## Evening Session: OS Comparison Note (Windows vs macOS vs Linux, for servers)

**Windows Server** — Familiar GUI, strong Active Directory/enterprise integration, but heavier resource footprint and licensing costs. Common in corporate environments running .NET or SQL Server workloads.

**macOS** — Rarely used as a server OS in production; Apple doesn't really support it for that role anymore. Mostly relevant for local dev/testing, not cloud infrastructure.

**Linux** — Dominant choice for cloud/DevOps: free, lightweight, highly configurable, huge ecosystem (Docker, Kubernetes, most cloud CLI tools assume Linux). Almost every AWS EC2 instance, container, and CI/CD pipeline runs on it.

**Takeaway for a server:** Linux wins on cost, performance, and ecosystem fit for cloud/DevOps work; Windows Server has its place in enterprise shops; macOS isn't really a server contender.
